{"id":"2ec0511903e19292","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-thm-spectral-theorem.md","title":"Spectral Theorem","display":"thm-spectral-theorem — Spectral Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-spectral-theorem","aliases":["58-thm-spectral-theorem"],"display":"thm-spectral-theorem — Spectral Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-self-adjoint]]","[[58-df-adjoint]]","[[58-df-projection-valued]]","[[58-df-hilbert-space]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-spectral-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-spectral-theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-spectral-theorem — Spectral Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5998e080b5d378a0\" href=\"?note=5998e080b5d378a0\" title=\"58-df-self-adjoint\">58-df-self-adjoint</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"58-df-adjoint\">58-df-adjoint</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"71f1954115db03be\" href=\"?note=71f1954115db03be\" title=\"58-df-projection-valued\">58-df-projection-valued</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H\">\\(H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H\\)</span> (Hilbert-space carrier, inner product, scalar field, addition, and scalar multiplication, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> (self-adjoint operator on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5998e080b5d378a0\" href=\"?note=5998e080b5d378a0\" title=\"58-df-self-adjoint\">58-df-self-adjoint</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\">\\(\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\)</span> (Borel sigma-algebra of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\)</span> (Hilbert-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\\)</span> (adjoint-operator predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"58-df-adjoint\">58-df-adjoint</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PVMStructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PVMStructure}_S\\)</span> (projection-valued-measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"71f1954115db03be\" href=\"?note=71f1954115db03be\" title=\"58-df-projection-valued\">58-df-projection-valued</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}spectral\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\exists T^\\ast\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S(T,T^\\ast,H,B,H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land T=T^\\ast\\bigr)\\to\\exists E\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{PVMStructure}_S(E,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R),H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land T=\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda\\,dE_\\lambda\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}spectral\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\exists T^\\ast\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S(T,T^\\ast,H,B,H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land T=T^\\ast\\bigr)\\to\\exists E\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{PVMStructure}_S(E,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R),H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land T=\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda\\,dE_\\lambda\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The antecedent fixes the full Hilbert-space structure and expresses self-adjointness through the explicit adjoint relation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T=T^\\ast\">\\(T=T^\\ast\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The resulting projection-valued measure is carried by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>; its support is concentrated on the spectrum of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>, so the integral over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span> is the standard spectral representation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-self-adjoint","status":"resolved","id":"5998e080b5d378a0","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-self-adjoint]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-adjoint","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-adjoint]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-projection-valued","status":"resolved","id":"71f1954115db03be","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-projection-valued]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H$ (Hilbert-space carrier, inner product, scalar field, addition, and scalar multiplication, see [[58-df-hilbert-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-self-adjoint","status":"resolved","id":"5998e080b5d378a0","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$T$ (self-adjoint operator on $H$, see [[58-df-self-adjoint]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S$ (Hilbert-space predicate, see [[58-df-hilbert-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-adjoint","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S$ (adjoint-operator predicate, see [[58-df-adjoint]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-projection-valued","status":"resolved","id":"71f1954115db03be","anchor":"ref-9","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PVMStructure}_S$ (projection-valued-measure predicate, see [[58-df-projection-valued]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PVMStructure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}spectral\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\exists T^\\ast\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S(T,T^\\ast,H,B,H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land T=T^\\ast\\bigr)\\to\\exists E\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{PVMStructure}_S(E,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R),H,B,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land T=\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda\\,dE_\\lambda\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"T=T^\\ast","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false}],"bytes":1638,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4430","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-thm-spectral-theorem.md|58-thm-spectral-theorem]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["5998e080b5d378a0","200eacd293b1282b","71f1954115db03be","b70ce791d5b1a19b"]}